\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces NutriBiteBot system architecture. Model development (top) is performed offline on credentialed data. In the local deployment, allergy, intolerance and preference exclusions are applied first, followed by TabNet risk stratification, rule-based portion computation, and recipe generation whose output is accepted only if a deterministic verifier passes it (otherwise regenerated, then replaced by a template). Only the refrigerator image (to Roboflow) and the comorbidity flags, permitted ingredients with gram ceilings and avoid-names (to Groq) leave the local boundary (dashed); the exclusion list stays local; optional records are kept in a local Supabase database.}}{8}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{8}{NutriBiteBot system architecture. Model development (top) is performed offline on credentialed data. In the local deployment, allergy, intolerance and preference exclusions are applied first, followed by TabNet risk stratification, rule-based portion computation, and recipe generation whose output is accepted only if a deterministic verifier passes it (otherwise regenerated, then replaced by a template). Only the refrigerator image (to Roboflow) and the comorbidity flags, permitted ingredients with gram ceilings and avoid-names (to Groq) leave the local boundary (dashed); the exclusion list stays local; optional records are kept in a local Supabase database}{figure.caption.4}{}}
